.TH RESCOMP 1 "2026-10-12" "ASL 1.42.313" "Development Tools"
.SH NAME
rescomp \- compile AS message resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rescomp
INPUT.mes [\-m OUTPUT.msg] [\-h OUTPUT.rsc] [\-i OUTPUT.msh]
.br
.B rescomp
INPUT.mes OUTPUT.msg [OUTPUT.rsc [OUTPUT.msh]]
.br
.B rescomp \-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
A host build tool generated in the build directory, not an installed
runtime executable. CMake invokes it automatically to generate localized
catalogs and headers. Explicit output flags avoid ambiguity in the legacy
positional order. Multiple output types can be generated together.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m file
Write an external binary message catalog.
.TP
.B \-h file
Write a C header assigning indices to messages.
.TP
.B \-i file
Write a C header containing embedded catalog bytes.
.TP
.B \-help
Print syntax and exit successfully. With no arguments, syntax is printed
to stderr and the program exits with status 1. This tool does not implement
the runtime programs' \-version or preset-environment options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
build/rescomp as.mes \-m output.msg \-h output.rsc \-i output.msh
.fi
.PP
Use the matching configuration directory and .exe suffix for a Windows
multi-configuration build.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asl (1)
.PP
The source-maintenance chapter of the AS manual describes .mes syntax.
